[Applause]  and the spirit award for best screenplay  goes to  maggie jillian all for the last daughter  this is maggie gyllenhaal's first spirit  award win she was previously nominated  for two awards for her performances in  the film's happy endings and secretary  tonight she is also nominated for best  director and  best feature film  thank you so much thank you writers  for welcoming me into your community and  the other writers in my category we did  a panel together just the other day and  we are all in love i think and um maybe  all of us especially with janix bravo  um i don't know who's not in love with  her  um  i see  and i feel that there is a real  conscious effort being made to make  space for different perspectives and  voices and i know that i have been the  beneficiary of that  my film is in an unusual language it's  the language of the minds of women  i've been sort of afraid to say that  because my film is not just for women  it's for everyone  but  as soon as i was born i learned to speak  the language of the men who were running  the world around me it was a matter of  survival but it was also very  interesting like learning any language  and it meant that i could understand the  roots and the subtleties of a lot of  great movies  so i'm suggesting  that there can be a real pleasure in  learning a language that's not your  native one  like learning french or italian and the  the doors that it can open for you and  also  that there can be if it doesn't freak  you out a real pleasure in learning and  seeing something new  even if it doesn't look the way you  expect it to or the way that you wish it  thank you to the brilliant elena  ferrante and her translator ann  goldstein who gave me access to her work  thank you miss verante for knowing that  in your own words the effort of  adaptation requires not faithfulness but  invention and often betrayal  i think she means a sexy interactive  kind of betrayal  thank you to all my brutally honest and  loving readers netflix  you are a home for artists what a  beautiful partnership this has been  thank you  and to endeavor nagin charlie alex  kristen i was never backed into a corner  not once instead i was encouraged and  supported all the way through thank you  to my editor alfonso goncalves who is  here i think  and to my my brilliant dp helen louvard  also to my producers talia kleinhandler  and us not hendelson koran you were the  only people on my set i ever fought with  and that was be and only now and then  and that was because you were the very  closest to me my sisters and my partners  and thank you to my daughters i'm almost  done i know i thank you to my daughters  who made me a mother and helped me  understand the deepest and most  rewarding connection in the world  without whom i never would have been  able to make this movie and thank you to  my brilliant actors paul ed jack ali  jagmara dakota jesse olivia  i love all the ways that you in turn  betrayed my adaptation and gave it its  lifeblood  and one more actor who is  my favorite  my husband peter sarsgaard  who  has read almost every single draft heard  all the fucking music cues  taken our kids to the dentist put them  to bed fed them breakfast held my hand  in venice when we saw the movie for the  first time but most importantly who has  taught me the beauty and the thrill of  the real thing  as opposed to the fantasy  and that was my north star making this  movie  thank you  [Music]  [Applause]

